Adds opt-in `--resolution-threads N` for dependency-ready parallel module resolution,
deterministically ordered diagnostics, semantic module keys and module-qualified
generated names. Boogie state and snapshot identifiers are stable under unrelated
source movement, with counterexample locations rebound for the current invocation.
Editor resolution caches retain complete dependency-local worker outputs keyed by
module identity, with canonical builtin views and containment rebound on publication.
Whole-program admission is rerun after cache hits. Rejected resolver configurations
report their diagnostics without traversing unresolved translation inputs.
Operator export views recognize canonical builtin identities without relaxing
visibility checks on user declarations.
The default resolution path is unchanged.
